{"name":"Electrify","hex":"#5665a0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"electrify","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To supply electricity to; to charge with electricity.","To cause electricity to pass through; to affect by electricity; to give an electric shock to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electrify"}],"entries":[{"title":"Electrify (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Electrify\" is a song by British DJ and producer Jakwob. The song, lyrics written by Rocky Nti, James Jacob and Steve 'Dub' Jones was released as a single on 2 March 2012 as a digital download in the United Kingdom. It features vocals from Jetta, and incorporates sample replays of Indian music recreated by UK producer Mark Summers of SCORCCiO Sample Replays."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d8/ElectrifyJakwob.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrify_(song)","wikidata":"Q5357887"},{"title":"Electrification","blocks":[{"text":"Electrification is the process of powering by electricity and, in many contexts, the introduction of such power by changing over from an earlier power source. In the context of history of technology and economic development, electrification refers to the build-out of the electricity generation and electric power distribution systems. In the context of sustainable energy, electrification refers to the build-out of super grids and smart grids with distributed energy resources to accommodate the energy transition to renewable energy and the switch of end-uses to electricity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/China_electrification_surpasses_OECD.svg/330px-China_electrification_surpasses_OECD.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrification","wikidata":"Q1076056"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org